# Streaming Responses Implementation ✅

## Overview

Juno implements **real-time streaming responses** where AI-generated text appears progressively as the model generates it, rather than showing the complete response at the end. This provides immediate user feedback and a more natural conversation experience.

## Architecture

### Backend Streaming Pipeline
1. **Anthropic API Integration**: [anthropic.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers/anthropic.rs) handles Server-Sent Events (SSE)
2. **Event Emission**: [tool_logger.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/tool_logger.rs) emits streaming events to frontend
3. **Agent Coordination**: [agent_runner.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/implementations/agent_runner.rs) manages streaming detection

### Frontend Streaming Handlers
- **Event Listeners**: [App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx) contains three streaming event handlers
- **Progressive UI Updates**: Text chunks are appended to conversation in real-time
- **Duplicate Prevention**: Time-based duplicate detection prevents multiple responses

## Key Components

### Backend Events ([constants.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/constants.rs))
```rust
pub const AGENT_STREAM_START: &str = "agent-stream-start";
pub const AGENT_TEXT_STREAM: &str = "agent-text-stream"; 
pub const AGENT_STREAM_END: &str = "agent-stream-end";
```

### Frontend Event Types ([App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx))
```typescript
type StreamingTextEvent = { chunk: string; message_id?: string; };
type StreamStartEvent = { message_id: string; };
type StreamEndEvent = { message_id: string; complete_text: string; };
```

### Message Tracking
- **Unique IDs**: Each streaming session gets a unique `message_id`
- **Streaming State**: Messages have `isStreaming: boolean` field
- **Progressive Content**: Content builds up chunk by chunk

## Implementation Details

### 1. Stream Detection ([agent_runner.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/implementations/agent_runner.rs))
```rust
// Automatically detects if brain supports streaming
if brain.supports_streaming() {
    // Use streaming mode
    result = brain.decide_next_action_streaming(&messages, message_id).await?;
} else {
    // Fallback to standard mode
    result = brain.decide_next_action(&messages).await?;
}
```

### 2. SSE Parsing ([anthropic.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/agent/providers/anthropic.rs))
```rust
// Parse Server-Sent Events from Anthropic API
if line.starts_with("event: content_block_delta") {
    // Extract and emit text chunks
    emit_streaming_text_chunk(app_handle, &chunk, &message_id).await?;
}
```

### 3. Frontend Event Handling ([App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx))
```typescript
// Stream start: Create new message
const streamStartListener = listen<StreamStartEvent>("agent-stream-start", (event) => {
    const streamingMessage: ChatMessage = {
        role: "assistant", content: "", isStreaming: true, messageId: message_id
    };
    setConversation(prev => [...prev, streamingMessage]);
});

// Stream text: Update message content
const streamTextListener = listen<StreamingTextEvent>("agent-text-stream", (event) => {
    setConversation(prev => prev.map(msg => 
        msg.messageId === message_id && msg.isStreaming
            ? { ...msg, content: msg.content + chunk }
            : msg
    ));
});
```

## Duplicate Prevention

### Problem
Backend emits both streaming events AND final response event, causing duplicate messages.

### Solution: Time-Based Detection
```typescript
// Check for identical content within last 2 seconds
const isRecentlyStreamed = prevConversation.some(msg =>
    msg.role === "assistant" &&
    msg.content === response.text &&
    msg.timestamp && (now - msg.timestamp) < 2000
);
```

## TTS Integration

### During Streaming
- **Backend Handles TTS**: Anthropic brain generates TTS during streaming
- **Frontend Skips Audio**: No audio playback from frontend during streaming

### Non-Streaming Fallback  
- **Frontend Plays TTS**: For non-streaming providers, frontend handles audio

